    <Folder>
      <name>Owner-confirmed mission placemarks</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Christiansted Harbor Seaplane Base</name>
        <description>Victor Two Bravo infiltrates the mission-relevant portion of the Christiansted Harbor seaplane base to commandeer a floatplane for the approximately 39-mile north-northwest flight to East McFarlane Island. The operation is controlled through a Goldberg-linked shell aerial-tour company. Its seven armed contractors knowingly support Goldberg's covert transport and human-trafficking logistics. Four fixed alarm buttons, radios carried by all seven guards and the manager, and four static cameras form the compound security network. A full alarm causes all surviving armed guards to search for and shoot Victor Two Bravo on sight.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7077065,17.7471149,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Final pre-operational staging point — SUV</name>
        <description>Victor Two Bravo relocates the SUV to this short-duration staging point shortly before infiltration. The team transfers equipment and prepares to execute the plan after dark, having completed the longer observation and planning phase from the western beachside position. They do not remain here for hours conducting surveillance.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7067656,17.7466606,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Safehouse location</name>
        <description>The mission begins in an interactive, free-movement safehouse occupying the second-story residential space of this building. Victor Two Bravo reviews the East McFarlane lead, prepares equipment, and departs in the SUV.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7068125,17.7439375,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Seaplane-base administration building</name>
        <description>Victor Two Bravo infiltrates the compound and must bypass, incapacitate, restrain, or neutralize as required seven Goldberg-linked armed contractors: one at the east gate, one at the west gate, one patrolling the east berth, one patrolling the north jetty, one inside the north service entrance and first-floor corridor, and two accompanying the manager in his first-floor office. Fixed alarms are positioned at the north service entrance and in the manager's-office hallway; the gatehouses contain two more. The manager monitors four static CCTV feeds from his office. If all seven guards are eliminated before the manager is secured, he locks the office, calls the police, and forces a timed breach-and-key-recovery branch before land and maritime responders arrive.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7077841,17.7468758,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Found FBA-2C floatplane — north jetty</name>
        <description>The fueled Found FBA-2C that Victor Two Bravo commandeers for the flight to East McFarlane Island. Access is controlled through the manager and aircraft keys; the aircraft does not require a prolonged refueling sequence before departure. During the external-response branch, police pressure closes the land approaches while an armed U.S. Coast Guard patrol boat approaches this departure area.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7079045,17.7475921,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>East McFarlane covert landing and SINS handoff</name>
        <description>Smoke completes the final approach with the Found FBA-2C's engine shut down and lands at the same unlit, disused boat-launch entry point used at the opening of SINS OF OUR FATHERS. This coordinate is normalized to the controlling SINS mission map.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.8228542,18.2980253,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>North-jetty guard position</name>
        <description>One armed contractor patrols the north jetty and adjacent aircraft-berth area. His movement periodically carries him close to the Found FBA-2C, creating a timing problem during the final movement from the administration building to the aircraft. He carries a radio that can alert the other security personnel on base.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7079326,17.7473933,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>East-gate guard position</name>
        <description>One armed contractor remains near the tailgate of a white pickup truck just inside the east gate. Unless suspicious or alerted, he seldom moves far from the vehicle and is periodically distracted by texting and smoking. He can use either his radio or the alarm button inside the east gatehouse. The outward-facing east-gate camera creates a separate detection risk.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7082391,17.7466371,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>West-gate guard position</name>
        <description>One armed contractor spends most of his shift seated inside the west-gate office, visible through its window, watching football on television. He occasionally enters the administration building through the north service entrance to use the bathroom, returning after about three minutes. Roughly once every ten minutes, he also steps outside for about two minutes to look at the sky and take a small surreptitious swig from a hidden liquor flask. These absences create distinct infiltration windows. He retains his radio, the gatehouse alarm remains active, and the outward-facing west-gate camera continues watching the approach while he is away.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7074381,17.7469962,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>East-berth guard position</name>
        <description>One armed contractor patrols the east jetty and frequently pauses to look north over the water. At intervals he walks south to the open bay door on the north side of the administration building, enters the small break room immediately east of the bay, gets coffee, and returns outside. This routine creates a temporary gap in east-side observation. He carries a radio that can alert the other security personnel on base.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7081056,17.7471067,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Manager's office</name>
        <description>The first-floor office contains the shell-company manager, two armed contractors, the aircraft keys, and the CCTV monitoring station for all four static cameras. If the manager observes Victor Two Bravo on camera, he radios the nearest available guard to investigate. Under the normal route, the team secures the office, restrains the manager, and compels him to surrender the keys. If all seven guards are eliminated first, he locks himself inside and calls the police, forcing the player to breach the office and recover the keys before responders arrive.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7077755,17.7467519,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>North-service-entrance guard position</name>
        <description>One armed contractor is usually seated at a table immediately inside the northern service entrance, facing partly away from the doorway. He may walk the first-floor corridor and occasionally steps outside the service entrance for several minutes to smoke. He can use either his radio or the alarm button beside the north service entrance to alert the rest of the base.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7076779,17.7469794,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Alarm button — north service entrance</name>
        <description>One of four fixed compound alarm buttons. It is mounted beside the north main administration-building service entrance. Activating it places the surviving armed guards into the compound-wide shoot-on-sight alert state. The exact wall position is schematic until the administration-building floor plan is authored.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7076779,17.7469794,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Alarm button — east gatehouse</name>
        <description>One of four fixed compound alarm buttons. It is located inside the east gate gatehouse. Activating it places the surviving armed guards into the compound-wide shoot-on-sight alert state. Its point is schematic at this map scale.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7082391,17.7466371,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Alarm button — west gatehouse</name>
        <description>One of four fixed compound alarm buttons. It is located inside the west gate gatehouse. Activating it places the surviving armed guards into the compound-wide shoot-on-sight alert state. Its point is schematic at this map scale.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7074381,17.7469962,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Alarm button — manager's-office hallway</name>
        <description>One of four fixed compound alarm buttons. It is mounted in the first-floor hallway leading to the manager's office. Activating it places the surviving armed guards into the compound-wide shoot-on-sight alert state. The exact interior coordinate is schematic until the administration-building floor plan is authored.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7077420,17.7468550,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Security camera — east gate exterior</name>
        <description>Static camera mounted at the east gatehouse and aimed outward through the gate approach. The manager monitors this feed from the CCTV station in his office. A confirmed sighting causes him to radio the nearest available guard to investigate rather than immediately triggering the full compound alarm. The exact mount and field of view are schematic.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7082391,17.7466371,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Security camera — west gate exterior</name>
        <description>Static camera mounted at the west gatehouse and aimed outward through the gate approach. The manager monitors this feed from the CCTV station in his office. A confirmed sighting causes him to radio the nearest available guard to investigate rather than immediately triggering the full compound alarm. The exact mount and field of view are schematic.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7074381,17.7469962,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Security camera — fuel storage coverage one</name>
        <description>First of two static cameras providing overlapping surveillance of the fuel-storage area just southeast of the north jetty. The manager monitors the feed from his office and radios the nearest available guard if Victor Two Bravo is observed. Exact fuel-storage geometry, mount height, and sight cone remain schematic.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7076750,17.7472050,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Security camera — fuel storage coverage two</name>
        <description>Second static camera providing an overlapping angle on the fuel-storage area southeast of the north jetty. The manager monitors the feed from his office and radios the nearest available guard if Victor Two Bravo is observed. Exact fuel-storage geometry, mount height, and sight cone remain schematic.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1750-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7075900,17.7472900,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Long-duration surveillance position — SUV</name>
        <description>Victor Two Bravo drives from the safehouse to this beachside location west of the seaplane base and conceals the SUV near the vegetation-covered area. The team covertly observes activity in and around the compound before finalizing the infiltration plan. The passage of several hours is diegetically compressed rather than played in real time.</description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-0288D1</styleUrl>
        <Point><coordinates>-64.7099133,17.7471562,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
  </Document>
</kml>
